# Langfive — environment variables
#
# There is no root .env. Each app owns its own, because the three have
# genuinely different trust levels and a single shared file is how they drift:
#
#   apps/web/.env         <- NEXT_PUBLIC_*  PUBLIC, inlined into the JS bundle
#   apps/extension/.env   <- REACT_APP_*    PUBLIC, shipped inside the .zip
#   apps/api/.env         <- SECRET, server-side only
#
# Set them up:
#
#   cp apps/web/.env.sample       apps/web/.env
#   cp apps/extension/.env.sample apps/extension/.env
#   cp apps/api/.env.sample       apps/api/.env
#
# then fill in the blanks. Each .env.sample documents what its values do and
# where to get them.
#
# The one rule that matters: the Supabase service_role key and the R2
# credentials belong in apps/api/.env and nowhere else. Both web and extension
# ship their entire environment to users.
